    <string name="help_text"><b>What does the app do?</b>\nA home-screen widget with your next appointments, optionally with contact birthdays and open tasks.\n\n<b>Setup</b>\n1. Allow calendar access.\n2. Choose the calendars to show.\n3. \"Add widget to home screen\" or place it via the launcher widget list.\n\n<b>Settings</b>\nNumber of events and days, location, font, size and colours apply to the widget being edited; the preview shows the result. Tapping an event opens it in the calendar.\n\n<b>Tasks</b>\nSources: the free app Tasks.org (Google Tasks, Microsoft To Do, CalDAV), OpenTasks (CalDAV via DAVx⁵) and on-premises Exchange via EWS. Choose them under \"Configure task sources\".\n\n<b>Calendar colors</b>\nGoogle calendars use the Google palette and send the color to Google. Exchange and local calendars keep it on this device only; \"Keep own colors\" puts it back after a sync resets it.\n\n<b>Save / load</b>\nThe icons at the top save the display settings to a JSON file (e.g. in Drive, for moving to a new phone) and load them again. The last file is remembered; saving again asks whether to overwrite it. Calendars and task lists are chosen again on each phone.</string>
    <string name="btn_calendar_colors">Change calendar colors</string>
    <string name="help_calendar_colors">Changes the color for all calendar apps. Google calendars use the Google palette and sync the color to Google; other calendars keep it on this device only.</string>
    <string name="restore_colors">Keep own colors</string>
    <string name="help_restore_colors">Sets Exchange and local calendar colors again after a sync resets them.</string>
